text Help_Text_AnswerPlayingForFirstTime {
    "You become the main character,\n"
    "exploring the world of Pokémon.\l"
    "By talking to people and solving\l"
    "mysteries, new paths will open to you.\l"
    "Strive for the goal together with your\l"
    "wonderful Pokémon.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatShouldIBeDoing {
    "When you come across another person,\n"
    "go up to them and press the A Button.\l"
    "That will get them to talk and interact\l"
    "with your character. You may also\l"
    "examine various items and objects in\l"
    "the same way. Talk to people and check\l"
    "things often to obtain information.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerCantGetOutOfRoom {
    "On the stairs or the exits of a\n"
    "building is a red mat. Move your\l"
    "character to stand on top of the\l"
    "red mat. Press the {PLUS} Control Pad \l"
    "toward the stairs or the exit to\l"
    "advance.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerCantFindPersonIWant {
    "This isn't something you should worry\n"
    "about too much.\l"
    "Talk to other people, check signs,\l"
    "check things, and so on.\l"
    "Sometimes, you may need to just move\l"
    "to a new town or place.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerTalkedToEveryoneNowWhat {
    "Try moving on to a new road, town, or\n"
    "place.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerSomeoneBlockingMyWay {
    "There could be something in the town\n"
    "or inside a building that is the cause.\l"
    "Try talking to the people in the area\l"
    "again. If there is a problem that they\l"
    "need solved, you may have to help.\l"
    "Afterwards, try talking to the person\l"
    "blocking your way again.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerICantGoOn {
    "Try talking to people by going up to\n"
    "them and pressing the A Button.\l"
    "Also, try checking things like odd trees\l"
    "and strange rocks with the A Button.\l"
    "Press the {PLUS} Control Pad and try going\l"
    "to places that look impassable, too.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerOutOfThingsToDo {
    "Try going to places where you \n"
    "haven't visited yet.\l"
    "Also, check everything that looks\l"
    "suspicious by pressing the A Button.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatHappenedToItemIGot {
    "Any item that you are given by another\n"
    "character goes in your Bag.\l"
    "The item is automatically sorted and\l"
    "placed in one of three pockets.\l"
    "For instructions on the Bag's use,\l"
    "please refer to the Help System's\l"
    "“How do I do this?” heading.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatAreMyAdventureBasics {
    "If Pokémon are hurt in battle,\n"
    "take them to a Pokémon Center and\l"
    "have them healed by the staff.\l"
    "Get in the habit of saving your\l"
    "game and recording your progress.\l"
    "Stock up on healing items at\l"
    "Pokémon Marts before traveling far.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerHowAreRoadsForestsDifferent {
    "Forests are basically the same as\n"
    "roads but they can be like mazes.\l"
    "All forests have a way out, so don't\l"
    "give up if you get lost.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerHowAreCavesDifferent {
    "Caves are dark and dangerous. Wild\n"
    "Pokémon can appear anywhere in them.\l"
    "If there is an emergency, rush to a\l"
    "Pokémon Center or use items.\l"
    "New towns await discovery beyond some\l"
    "caves, so don't give up.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerHowDoIProgress {
    "The object of the game is to train\n"
    "your Pokémon and move forward.\l"
    "You must collect info and solve\l"
    "problems. For example, what do you\l"
    "need to get around an obstacle?\l"
    "What would get that impeding\l"
    "person out of the way?$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhenCanIUseItem {
    "There are several kinds of items.\n"
    "Some can be used only on the field.\l"
    "Some are only for use during battle.\l"
    "Some can be used anytime.\l"
    "Try using an item - if it can't be used,\l"
    "you will be alerted.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatsABattle {
    "In a battle, Pokémon try to reduce\n"
    "one another's vitality, expressed as\l"
    "HP. If a Pokémon's HP falls to zero,\l"
    "it faints, and the other Pokémon\l"
    "wins. By winning a battle, Pokémon\l"
    "earn EXP. Points, which help them\l"
    "level up (grow stronger).$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerHowDoIPrepareForBattle {
    "First, fully heal the Pokémon in your\n"
    "party (the Pokémon with you) at any\l"
    "Pokémon Center.\l"
    "You should also buy healing items for\l"
    "emergencies at a Pokémon Mart.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatIsAMonsVitality {
    "A Pokémon's vitality is expressed in HP.\n"
    "If a Pokémon is hurt in battle, HP is\l"
    "subtracted. If its HP drops to zero,\l"
    "the Pokémon faints.\l"
    "Heal hurt or fainted Pokémon at a\l"
    "Pokémon Center or by using items.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerMyMonsAreHurt {
    "A Pokémon Center is like an inn for\n"
    "Pokémon. It will fully heal Pokémon of\l"
    "any status problems and fully restore\l"
    "their HP using a special machine.\l"
    "This service is free, so get in the\l"
    "habit of healing your Pokémon often.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatIsStatusProblem {
    "A status problem refers to an ailment\n"
    "that is inflicted on a Pokémon by its\l"
    "foe's attack. These include burns,\l"
    "paralysis, poisoning, sleep, and\l"
    "freezing. These can be healed by\l"
    "visiting a Pokémon Center or using\l"
    "the appropriate item.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatHappensIfAllMyMonsFaint {
    "If all the Pokémon in your party\n"
    "(all the Pokémon with you) faint, you\l"
    "lose some Money, and you are\l"
    "returned home or to a Pokémon\l"
    "Center. To reduce that chance, visit\l"
    "Pokémon Centers often. Also, get\l"
    "in the habit of saving often.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerCantCatchMons {
    "If a wild Pokémon escapes from a Poké\n"
    "Ball, it's obviously still feisty.\l"
    "Try reducing its HP some more, and\l"
    "try to weaken it with paralysis or sleep\l"
    "before trying to catch it.\l"
    "If the Poké Ball rocks for a while,\l"
    "the quarry is close to being caught!$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerRanOutOfPotions {
    "There are shops, known as Pokémon\n"
    "Marts, that sell items.\l"
    "You will not find Pokémon Marts on\l"
    "roads, in forests, or in caves.\l"
    "Stock up on needed items while you are\l"
    "visiting a town with a Pokémon Mart.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerCanIBuyPokeBalls {
    "You may buy Poké Balls at any\n"
    "Pokémon Mart in any town.\l"
    "You will not find Pokémon Marts on\l"
    "roads, in forests, or in caves.\l"
    "Stock up on Poké Balls while you are\l"
    "visiting a town with a Pokémon Mart.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatsATrainer {
    "A Trainer is a person who raises\n"
    "Pokémon through battling.\l"
    "Trainers will challenge you \l"
    "wherever they are - it could be on\l"
    "a road, in forests, caves, anywhere.\l"
    "If your eyes meet, you have to accept\l"
    "their challenge. So be careful!$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerHowDoIWinAgainstTrainer {
    "To beat a Trainer in battle, use\n"
    "Pokémon that have type advantages\l"
    "over the foe's Pokémon. You may also\l"
    "use highly trained Pokémon with\l"
    "overwhelming power. Outnumbering the\l"
    "foe's Pokémon is another obvious\l"
    "tactic.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhereDoMonsAppear {
    "Wild Pokémon will appear in tall grass,\n"
    "on roads, and in forests. They will\l"
    "appear anywhere in dark caves.\l"
    "There are no wild Pokémon or Trainers\l"
    "in towns, so they are safe places.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatAreMoves {
    "Pokémon may learn up to four different\n"
    "techniques, or moves. There is a great\l"
    "variety of moves including attacks and\l"
    "those with special effects. The kinds\l"
    "of moves that can be learned vary\l"
    "for each Pokémon. Some moves\l"
    "can be learned from machines.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatAreHiddenMoves {
    "Hidden moves are those that are\n"
    "especially important for your\l"
    "adventure. To use such a move outside\l"
    "of battle, open the “Pokémon” Menu\l"
    "and make the Pokémon that knows the\l"
    "move use it. A fainted Pokémon may use\l"
    "a Hidden move outside of battle.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatMovesShouldIUse {
    "Select “Fight,” and the Menu of moves\n"
    "will appear. Consider the type\l"
    "matchups, and use the most effective\l"
    "moves. You can check the effects of\l"
    "moves by opening “Pokémon,”\l"
    "picking a Pokémon, opening “Summary,”\l"
    "then opening “Pokémon Skills.”$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWantToAddMoreMoves {
    "The most a Pokémon can learn is four\n"
    "moves. They are learned as the\l"
    "Pokémon levels up. It can also be\l"
    "taught a move using a TM (Technical\l"
    "Machine) or HM (Hidden Machine).\l"
    "There are also people who teach moves.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWantToMakeMonStronger {
    "The key to making your Pokémon\n"
    "strong is to battle and win often.\l"
    "The EXP. (Experience) Points earned\l"
    "by winning battles accumulate to\l"
    "level up Pokémon that participated in\l"
    "them. Battle wild Pokémon often to\l"
    "level up your party.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerFoeMonsTooStrong {
    "If your foes are too strong, try\n"
    "leveling up your Pokémon some more.\l"
    "Go back the way you came and battle\l"
    "wild Pokémon to level up your party.\l"
    "You may also battle Trainers whom you\l"
    "have not battled before.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatDoIDoInCave {
    "Unlike roads and forests, wild Pokémon\n"
    "can appear anywhere in caves.\l"
    "If your Pokémon are hurt in a cave,\l"
    "rush to a Pokémon Center or use items\l"
    "to heal them right away. It is very\l"
    "dangerous to force your luck in caves.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerNothingIWantToKnow {
    "Trust your own knowledge and power.\n"
    "Believe in yourself and find your way!$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatsPokemonCenter {
    "A Pokémon Center is identified by its\n"
    "red roof and a “P.C” sign. Every\l"
    "Pokémon Center offers such services as\l"
    "fully healing Pokémon and free PC use,\l"
    "making it essential for your travels.\l"
    "On the upper floor are facilities for\l"
    "linking with friends and others.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatsPokemonMart {
    "A Pokémon Mart is identified by its\n"
    "blue roof and a “Mart” sign.\l"
    "Items can be bought and sold at any\l"
    "Pokémon Mart. Some Marts carry items\l"
    "that are available only in their towns.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWantToEndGame {
    "You can safely end your game by\n"
    "selecting “Save” on the Menu.\l"
    "Once you have saved, the game can be\l"
    "safely turned off. When the game is\l"
    "turned back on, you can resume from\l"
    "where you last saved.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatsAMon {
    "Pokémon are living beings about which\n"
    "many mysteries still remain. You may\l"
    "see them in grass, the sea, and caves.\l"
    "They appear to obey the wishes of the\l"
    "Trainers that caught them.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatIsThatPersonLike {
    "Use the Fame Checker among the\n"
    "Key Items in your Bag.\l"
    "It may give you a hint, so try it out.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatDoesHiddenMoveDo {
    "A Hidden move is taught to a Pokémon\n"
    "using an HM (Hidden Machine).\l"
    "A Hidden move is important for helping\l"
    "your adventure. For example, one is\l"
    "used to light up dark caves. Another\l"
    "cuts down small trees. There is one\l"
    "for traveling on water, and so on.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatDoIDoInSafari {
    "Try to catch wild Pokémon by throwing\n"
    "the special Safari Balls.\l"
    "You may keep any item you find, too.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatAreSafariRules {
    "Your Safari Game ends once you have\n"
    "traveled a certain distance or thrown\l"
    "all your Safari Balls.\l"
    "Open the Menu to check the remaining\l"
    "number of steps and Safari Balls.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWantToEndSafari {
    "If you would like to cut your Safari\n"
    "Game short, open the Menu and select\l"
    "“Retire” at the top of the list.$"
}

text Help_Text_AnswerWhatIsAGym {
    "Pokémon Gyms are operated by the\n"
    "Pokémon League and are training\l"
    "facilities for Trainers. They are all\l"
    "across the land in cities and towns.\l"
    "Each one is headed by a Leader, who\l"
    "is a very skilled Trainer. Beat the\l"
    "Leader to collect a Badge.$"
}

