}

text Help_Text_Badges2 {
    "Badges$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineHP {
    "HP indicates a Pokémon's vitality.\n"
    "If a Pokémon's HP drops to zero, it\l"
    "faints and is unable to battle.\l"
    "So, the key in battle is to try to\l"
    "reduce the foe's HP to zero.\l"
    "If your Pokémon are hurt, restore their\l"
    "HP at a Pokémon Center or use items.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineEXP {
    "EXP. Points stands for “Experience\n"
    "Points.” Pokémon gain EXP. Points by\l"
    "participating in winning battles.\l"
    "When a Pokémon accumulates sufficient\l"
    "EXP. Points, it levels up. The EXP. Bar\l"
    "indicates accumulated EXP. Points.\l"
    "It returns to zero upon leveling up.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineMoves {
    "Pokémon may learn up to four different\n"
    "moves. There are many kinds of moves\l"
    "including attacks and those with\l"
    "special effects. The kinds of moves\l"
    "that can be learned vary for each\l"
    "Pokémon. Some moves can be learned\l"
    "from items.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineAttack {
    "Attack indicates the power of an\n"
    "offensive move. The higher this stat,\l"
    "the more powerful the move.\l"
    "It is applied for the following move\l"
    "types: Normal, Poison, Ground,\l"
    "Flying, Bug, Fighting, Rock, Ghost,\l"
    "and Steel.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineDefense {
    "Defense indicates the resistance a\n"
    "Pokémon has against physical attacks.\l"
    "The higher this stat, the less damage\l"
    "sustained from a foe's physical hit.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineSpAtk {
    "Sp. Atk (Special Attack) indicates the\n"
    "power of a special attack move.\l"
    "The higher this stat, the more powerful\l"
    "the special attack move.\l"
    "It is applied for the following move\l"
    "types: Fire, Water, Electric, Grass,\l"
    "Ice, Psychic, Dragon, and Dark.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineSpDef {
    "Sp. Def (Special Defense) indicates\n"
    "the resistance a Pokémon has against\l"
    "special attacks.\l"
    "The higher this stat, the less damage\l"
    "sustained from a foe's special attack.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineSpeed {
    "Speed indicates the agility of a\n"
    "Pokémon. If this stat exceeds the foe's\l"
    "in battle, the Pokémon can make a move\l"
    "before its slower opponent.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineLevel {
    "Lv. (Level) indicates the growth and\n"
    "strength of a Pokémon.\l"
    "In general, when a Pokémon levels up,\l"
    "its stats such as HP, Attack, and\l"
    "Defense rise, making it stronger.\l"
    "Pokémon may learn a new move upon\l"
    "leveling up.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineType {
    "Pokémon and moves are classified by\n"
    "type. Every type has advantageous and\l"
    "disadvantageous matchups against\l"
    "other types. For example, like a rock-\l"
    "paper-scissors game, the Water type is\l"
    "strong against the Fire type and weak\l"
    "against the Grass type.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineOT {
    "OT stands for “Original Trainer,”\n"
    "the first Trainer to have caught the\l"
    "selected Pokémon.\l"
    "Even if the Pokémon is traded, the OT\l"
    "name will remain unchanged.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineItem {
    "All Pokémon can be made to hold one\n"
    "item each. Some items will be used by\l"
    "the Pokémon automatically in certain\l"
    "situations. To make a Pokémon hold an\l"
    "item, select the item from the Bag and\l"
    "“Give” it to the Pokémon.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineAbility {
    "All Pokémon have a special Ability.\n"
    "There are many different kinds of these\l"
    "abilities, some used in battle, some\l"
    "elsewhere. The abilities differ from\l"
    "species to species. Some species may\l"
    "have more than one kind of ability.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineMoney {
    "Whenever you win a battle against a\n"
    "Trainer, you are given prize money.\l"
    "Save up your prize money so you can\l"
    "enjoy shopping at Pokémon Marts!$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineMoveType {
    "Moves are also classified by types.\n"
    "If a Pokémon of a certain type uses\l"
    "a move of the same type, the move's\l"
    "power is boosted. If the move's type\l"
    "has a matchup advantage against the\l"
    "target, its effectiveness is also\l"
    "boosted.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineNature {
    "All Pokémon have a personality,\n"
    "or “Nature.” The Pokémon's\l"
    "nature appears to affect how the\l"
    "Pokémon will grow upon leveling up.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineIDNo {
    "The ID No. is a special number assigned\n"
    "specifically to you as a Trainer.\l"
    "Together with the OT name, the ID No.\l"
    "is used to precisely identify the\l"
    "Original Trainer.\l"
    "The ID No. does not change even if the\l"
    "Pokémon is traded.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefinePP {
    "PP stands for “Power Points.”\n"
    "It indicates the number of times a\l"
    "certain move can be used in battle.\l"
    "Like HP, PP can be restored by visiting\l"
    "a Pokémon Center or using certain\l"
    "items.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefinePower {
    "Power indicates the strength of an\n"
    "attack. The higher this number, the\l"
    "greater the damage that can be\l"
    "inflicted on the foe!$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineAccuracy {
    "Accuracy indicates the probability of\n"
    "the move hitting the foe.\l"
    "The higher this number, the more likely\l"
    "the move will strike the target.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineFNT {
    "Fnt stands for “fainted.”\n"
    "A Pokémon faints if its HP is reduced\l"
    "to zero. It becomes incapable of taking\l"
    "part in battle.\l"
    "Restore a fainted Pokémon at a Pokémon\l"
    "Center, or use an item.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineItems {
    "Ordinary items bought at any Pokémon\n"
    "Mart are placed in the Items Pocket.\l"
    "Items may be used, given to a Pokémon\l"
    "to hold, or tossed out as garbage.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineKeyItems {
    "Important items that you find or \n"
    "receive from people are placed in the\l"
    "Key Items Pocket.\l"
    "Key items may be used, or registered\l"
    "for use instantly with Select. Once\l"
    "registered, the item can be used\l"
    "without opening the Menu and Bag.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefinePokeBalls {
    "Poké Balls, which are used for\n"
    "catching wild Pokémon, are placed in\l"
    "the Poké Balls Pocket.\l"
    "Poké Balls may be bought at Pokémon\l"
    "Marts. They may be used, given to a\l"
    "Pokémon to hold, or tossed out as\l"
    "garbage.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefinePokedex {
    "This indicates the number of species of\n"
    "Pokémon you have caught and/or\l"
    "evolved to fill the Pokédex.\l"
    "Try hard to catch all sorts of\l"
    "Pokémon!$"
}

text Help_Text_DefinePlayTime {
    "This is the total amount of time that\n"
    "you have played this game.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineBadges {
    "The Pokémon League Badges that you\n"
    "have won are registered and shown.\l"
    "Earn Badges by defeating Gym Leaders\l"
    "in various cities and towns.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineTextSpeed {
    "You can adjust how quickly the text is\n"
    "displayed. Choose one: Slow, Mid,\l"
    "or Fast.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineBattleScene {
    "You can choose to turn the battle\n"
    "animation On or Off.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineBattleStyle {
    "You can choose whether or not a\n"
    "Trainer can switch a Pokémon after\l"
    "it has made its foe faint.\l"
    "Set to “Shift” if you would like the\l"
    "chance to switch a Pokémon after it\l"
    "has made its foe faint.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineSound {
    "You can choose between Mono and\n"
    "Stereo sound output.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineButtonMode {
    "Set to “Help” to display help messages\n"
    "by pressing the L or R Button.\l"
    "Set to “LR” to enable the switching\l"
    "of the Pokédex pages and Bag Pockets\l"
    "using the L and R Buttons.\l"
    "Set to “L=A” to make the L Button\l"
    "work the same as the A Button.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineFrame {
    "You may choose the design of the frame\n"
    "around certain menus. Try them out and\l"
    "see what you like.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineCancel2 {
    "The settings will be changed to the\n"
    "selections shown in red, and you will\l"
    "return to the Menu.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineTM {
    "A TM (Technical Machine) is a device\n"
    "used to teach a move to a Pokémon.\l"
    "There are many different kinds.\l"
    "Moves can be taught only to those\l"
    "Pokémon capable of using them.\l"
    "A TM breaks after a single use.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineHM {
    "An HM (Hidden Machine) is a device used\n"
    "to teach a Hidden move to a Pokémon.\l"
    "A Hidden move can be taught only to\l"
    "those Pokémon capable of using it.\l"
    "Unlike a TM, an HM can be used over\l"
    "and over. A Hidden move can be tough\l"
    "for a Pokémon to forget.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineHMMove {
    "Hidden moves are those that are\n"
    "especially important for your\l"
    "adventure. To use such a move outside\l"
    "of battle, open the “Pokémon” Menu\l"
    "and make the Pokémon that knows the\l"
    "move use it. A fainted Pokémon may use\l"
    "a Hidden move outside of battle.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineEvolution {
    "Among Pokémon, there are some that\n"
    "undergo major changes (evolution) upon\l"
    "growing to certain levels. Evolution\l"
    "causes a Pokémon to alter form, change\l"
    "its name, and perhaps change the moves\l"
    "it may learn. Some Pokémon evolve\l"
    "due to reasons other than leveling up.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineStatusProblem {
    "Status problems include:\n"
    "Sleep: Can't use moves.\l"
    "Poison: Causes steady HP loss.\l"
    "Paralysis: May prevent moves.\l"
    "Burn: HP loss and lowers Attack.\l"
    "Freeze: Can't use moves.\l"
    "These can be healed with items, etc.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefinePokemon {
    "Pokémon is a name given to describe\n"
    "wondrous creatures that inhabit all\l"
    "corners of this world.\l"
    "People raise Pokémon to be their pets,\l"
    "use them for battling, and so on.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineIDNo2 {
    "The ID No. is a special number assigned\n"
    "specifically to you as a Trainer.\l"
    "Together with the OT name, the ID No.\l"
    "is used to precisely identify the\l"
    "Original Trainer.\l"
    "The ID No. does not change even if the\l"
    "Pokémon is traded.$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineMoney2 {
    "Whenever you win a battle against a\n"
    "Trainer, you are given prize money.\l"
    "Save up your prize money so you can\l"
    "enjoy shopping at Pokémon Marts!$"
}

text Help_Text_DefineBadges2 {
    "This indicates the number of Pokémon\n"
    "League Badges that you have won.\l"
    "Earn Badges by defeating Gym Leaders\l"
    "in various cities and towns.$"
}

text Help_Text_TheHelpSystem {
    "The Help System$"
}

text Help_Text_TheGame {
    "The game$"
}

text Help_Text_WirelessAdapter {
    "Wireless Adapter$"
}

text Help_Text_GameFundamentals1 {
    "Game fundamentals 1$"
}

text Help_Text_GameFundamentals2 {
    "Game fundamentals 2$"
}

text Help_Text_GameFundamentals3 {
    "Game fundamentals 3$"
}

text Help_Text_WhatArePokemon {
    "What are Pokémon?$"
}

text Help_Text_DescTheHelpSystem {
    "The help messages change depending on\n"
    "how much you have progressed in the\l"
    "game. They are designed to support you\l"
    "when you need them. If there is\l"
    "anything that you don't understand,\l"
    "please look up the Help System!$"
}

text Help_Text_DescTheGame {
    "You become the main character to\n"
    "explore the world of Pokémon!\l"
    "By talking to people and solving\l"
    "mysteries, new paths will open to you.\l"
    "Strive for the goal together with your\l"
    "wonderful Pokémon!$"
}

text Help_Text_DescWirelessAdapter {
    "This game communicates over a wireless\n"
    "link using the Wireless Adapter.\p"
    "Go wireless anywhere, anytime, and\n"
    "with anybody!\p"
    "Try playing with the Wireless Adapter\n"
    "always attached!$"
}

text Help_Text_DescGameFundamentals1 {
    "Visit every city and town, travel every\n"
    "road, explore every cave, and face\l"
    "every challenge as you strive to\l"
    "become the greatest Trainer of\l"
    "Pokémon!$"
}

text Help_Text_DescGameFundamentals2 {
    "On your adventure, you will be faced\n"
    "with many obstacles. Every obstacle\l"
    "can be overcome by doing something\l"
    "or by solving mysteries. Some obstacles\l"
    "are affected by something that happens\l"
    "far away.$"
}

text Help_Text_DescGameFundamentals3 {
    "Some of the obstacles in your way can\n"
    "be removed once your Pokémon learn\l"
    "specific moves.$"
}

text Help_Text_DescWhatArePokemon {
    "Pokémon are wondrous creatures that\n"
    "are shrouded in mystery. You may meet\l"
    "them all over the world…in tall\l"
    "grass, caves, the sea, and more.\l"
    "They appear to grow obedient to the\l"
    "Trainers that caught them.$"
}

